    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S002/text",
      "value": "For the other branch introduce L2: n≥1. Fix arbitrary q under L3: q>D, and arbitrary positive delta and epsilon. N002 gives D≥0, so q>0. Define r=min(1,delta/sqrt(2))>0; thus r≤1 and sqrt(2)r≤delta. By N001 applied to E, H^q(E)=0. The nonnegative content H^q_r(E) is at most this supremum, hence zero. The infimum defining that content therefore supplies a countable r-cover W with total q-cost<epsilon/2. The infimum is zero, so its admissible family is nonempty (an empty infimum is infinity); its defining approximation property gives the stated cover. This is the existence statement F001, before choosing W."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/@R004/argument/@S001/text",
      "value": "Under L1: n=0, N002 gives E=R^0 and D=0. The coordinate map from I to F obtained by adjoining the unique R^0 coordinate preserves all distances. Fix arbitrary a under L4: a>1. N003 gives H^a(I)=0, so by the defining infimum there are covers of I at every positive scale with arbitrarily small a-cost. Push these covers forward by that coordinate map; their diameters are unchanged, so H^a(F)=0. N001 gives dim_H(F)≤a. Let the arbitrary a decrease to 1 to obtain dim_H(F)≤1=D+1. Discharge L4 and L1 and record F000."
    },
